+                /*
+                 * Re-read the partition table only when the table on the disk
+                 * differs from the kernel's. A re-read removes and re-adds every
+                 * partition node, so a program that writes the whole disk and
+                 * then opens one of its partitions would find the node gone;
+                 * with the table unchanged, "change" for the disk and its
